From 9ebd6c4b3ec467e793c6e4342c2014a81eb45117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:30:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fs/aufs: pass const mnt_idmap and the LSM idmap for v7.4

v7.4 made struct mnt_idmap const through the vfs (merged in
00b04f4495c3 "Merge tag 'vfs-7.4-rc1.idmap'": the inode operations,
the vfs_*() helpers in e2f7f94b5a25, and mnt_idmap() itself in
025756ee7b47 "fs: port mnt_idmap() and file_mnt_idmap() to const
mnt_idmap"). aufs' inode operations no longer match the operation
tables, and the idmaps it gets from mnt_idmap() are now const.

v7.4 also added the mount idmap to the inode LSM hooks (16959c469f23
"lsm: expose mount idmaps to inode hooks"), so
security_inode_permission() takes it as its first argument:

  fs/aufs/i_op.c: error: too few arguments to function 'security_inode_permission'

Make every struct mnt_idmap pointer in aufs const, and pass the branch's
idmap (h_idmap, already used for the permission check above it) to
security_inode_permission(). None of the other inode hooks changed by
16959c469f23 are called by aufs.

Signed-off-by: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
